  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">xAI · Grok lab</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Grok Bot</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Named Bots on a cloud computer. This page covers only what xAI publishes about the Grok Bot product. It is not a Cursor internals note, and it is not Grok’s consumer multi-agent chat mode.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">What xAI publishes</h2>
    <p>Grok Bot is a named product: durable, named Bots (AI teammates) with jobs and context that persist. You work with a Bot by messaging it. Bots use a persistent cloud computer (browser, filesystem, terminal), connectors where available, and computer use for other apps and sites. Background work continues when the laptop is closed.</p>
    <p>Multiple Bots can run in parallel, message each other, and use group chats. They share <strong>one</strong> account-scoped computer. That computer is not a per-Bot security boundary — stated in the FAQ. Between users, isolation is described as strict.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Clients</h2>
    <p>Desktop: macOS, Windows, Linux. Mobile: iOS and Android. FAQ at launch: iPad not supported. Downloads are referenced via x.ai/bot on the get-started page.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access / billing</h2>
    <p>As published on docs (fetched 13 Sep 2026): included with every paid individual Cursor plan and with the Cursor Teams plan; you can also link an individual SuperGrok, SuperGrok Plus, or SuperGrok Heavy subscription. Usage described as weekly. Overview vs get-started matrices have differed slightly — cite the <a href="https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/overview">live overview</a> and the live plans page rather than hardcoding a stale card. Sign-in with a Cursor account / SuperGrok link is documented. Training and privacy follow applicable Cursor account settings per the FAQ. Do not expand that into unpublished Cursor architecture.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Skills vs routines</h2>
    <p>Skill = how to do a task. Routine = scheduled or event-driven assignment to a Bot (FAQ). Walk a Bot through a path once and it can save the path as a skill.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Not this product</h2>
    <p>Consumer Grok “multi-agent mode” on grok.com is a different surface. Grok Bot is not a physical robot. Stale secondary posts that called Grok Bot unconfirmed (Aug 2026 blogs) are superseded by docs.x.ai/grok-bot and x.ai/news (“Introducing Grok Bot”).</p>

